WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:06.310
Whether they're psychotic stalkers or pompous
jerks or just terrible decision-makers, significant

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.469
others in scary movies tend to cause a lot
more problems than they solve.

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:13.840
Let's take a look at the horror movie boyfriends
who were the absolute worst.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.220
There's obsessed, and then there's David McCall.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.780
In Fear, we're unfortunately introduced to
David, and he's any father's worst nightmare

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.660
right from the start.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.340
It takes him almost no time to start developing
an unhealthy infatuation with our leading

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.300
lady, the teenaged Nicole, and bucking any
attempts by her dad to keep him away from

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:31.800
her.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.940
Little by little, David starts to reveal how
unhinged and violent he is, harming everyone

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.460
from Nicole's best friend to a security guard
to the poor family dog.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.500
Despite all that he does to her loved ones,
though, he still somehow believes that he

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.160
and Nicole have a future together.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.640
Plus, he considers his lethal home invasion
plot to be a grand gesture that will lead

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.400
to a reunion.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.940
He's dangerous and deranged and completely
clueless about what women want.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.800
In other words: the full package.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.700
The idea of a high school teacher engaging
in an affair with a student, even if the student

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.420
is past the age of consent, is upsetting under
any circumstance.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.220
High school years are so formative and devoid
of responsible decision-making that it's inherently

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.400
dangerous and predatory for teachers to have
any personal relationship with students.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.440
So, The Boy Next Door's Claire definitely
deserves some scorn for sleeping with Noah,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:24.520
considering that he's her next-door neighbor,
her son's friend, and a student at her school.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.660
But after she decides to call it quits as
a result of the guilt and shame she feels

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.140
about it all, his overreaction is intense.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.930
Noah starts trying to win her back by vandalizing
the school wall with a lewd message about

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.520
their fling and blackmailing her with pictures
and a video of their tryst.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.980
When that doesn't work, he starts making threats
to her family, and all of this comes with

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:48.700
the explicit caveat that his aggression will
only end if she continues being his girlfriend.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:51.900
"No" definitely does not mean "no" for this
guy.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.900
"So it's time to make a choice my love - you
either live with me or you die with them"

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:05.659
Technically, "Hugh," a.k.a. Jeff Redmond,
isn't a horror movie boyfriend, but he is

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:07.700
a horror movie hookup gone horribly wrong.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.720
In It Follows, Hugh takes Jay out on a date,
first to the theater, and then to have a quick

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.220
drink.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:18.280
Ultimately, he manages to convince Jay that
he's an ordinary guy with no ulterior motive,

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.460
and the two wind up hooking up in the back
of his car.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.340
Once the deed is done, Hugh reveals the true
motive for his interest and advances.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.650
He's passing on to her a terrifying supernatural
entity in the hopes that she'll then pass

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.010
it along to someone else, et cetera, until
Hugh is so far removed from the chain that

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.080
he can live a long, worry-free life.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.260
The whole movie is a thinly-veiled metaphor
for the real-life threat of STDs, so Hugh's

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:46.860
decision to condemn Jay to a probable death
just to save his own skin is both indefensible

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.200
and one heck of a cinematic case for abstinence.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.940
To be fair to Paranormal Activity's Micah,
he really did have a point when he said that

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.001
Katie should've given him some kind of heads
up about her family's ghost curse before she

00:02:58.001 --> 00:02:58.700
moved in with him.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.340
That still doesn't excuse some of the stupid
and unhelpful things he does once a vengeful

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.440
spirit begins wreaking havoc on their home.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.680
For one thing, he has an annoyingly relentless
obsession with taping everything, but at least

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:14.880
that sets up a convenient plot device to help
frame the film in its signature found footage

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:15.380
style.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.180
The real problem with Micah is that he decides
it's a grand idea to taunt the demon that

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.300
has been haunting them.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.909
Then he ignores Katie's wishes by "borrowing"
a Ouija board, and of course all hell then

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:27.200
literally breaks loose.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:31.440
It's one thing that he goes all Blair Witch
Project on everything, but it's quite another

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.700
when he starts actively inviting trouble from
the mad poltergeist .

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.620
"No, you haven't been having progress and
you’re not in control it is in control and

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.020
if you think you’re in control you’re
being an idiot.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.440
Not a single thing you've done has helped."

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:49.720
Does a creepy internet stalker who pays a
girl to flirt actually qualify as a boyfriend?

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.020
The jury's still out on that one, but Tinker
is about as close as it gets in Cam.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:59.080
He seems to genuinely care about Alice, calling
her directly on a regular basis to chit-chat

00:03:59.099 --> 00:04:02.650
about her off-camera life and showering her
with tips and compliments.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.380
He even moves to her hometown to try and win
her over in real life.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.580
When the going gets tough, though, and Tinker
finds out that his favorite cam girl's feed

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:15.269
has been taken over by a computerized clone
version of her, he fails spectacularly to

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:17.500
intervene or even care very much.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.030
Instead of helping Alice in her hour of need,
he sneaks off to chat with the impersonator

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.479
who is making her life so hellish, because
all he really cares about is looking at Alice

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.800
online, in any form.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.480
It's bad enough that he takes the digital
adult entertainment game way too seriously,

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.560
but when he betrays Alice, that's when he
becomes truly disconnected.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:40.060
From the beginning of Scream, it's clear that
there's something not quite right with Skeet

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.540
Ulrich's Billy Loomis.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:46.520
With his shaggy hair, smouldering expressions,
and sense of entitlement, he doesn't do much

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.500
to hide the fact that he's a generic dirtbag
throughout the whole movie.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:54.240
What we don't find out until the end, though,
is just how thoroughly depraved he really

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:54.780
is.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:59.400
After successfully luring Sidney to give up
her virginity to him, Billy's free to then

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.820
let his partner-in-crime Stu take her out
now.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:05.600
It doesn't work, and she eventually finds
out that the two of them are responsible for

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.940
all of those phone calls and cat-and-mouse
games.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.300
Billy and Stu say it's all just revenge for
Sidney's mother breaking up the Loomis parents'

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.119
marriage and that they're just emulating scary
movies with their approach.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:20.540
Still, there's something particularly sinister
to Billy turning his relationship with Sidney

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.520
into a bedroom conquest that must be completed
before the killing can begin.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:28.040
On top of being a psycho killer, he's also
a sleaze.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:30.020
"What's the matter, Sidney?

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.360
You look like you’ve seen a ghost.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.919
Why are you doing this?

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:35.469
It’s all part of the game Sydney.

00:05:35.469 --> 00:05:37.360
"It's called 'Guess How I'm Gonna Die!'"

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:42.240
There's no doubt that the most abusive relationship
Sarah has in The Craft is with Nancy and the

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.380
pair of selfish sidekicks who enable her.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.840
However, Ulrich's Chris Hooker is a classic
case of creepy as well.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.580
Instead of trying to pursue a legitimate relationship
with Sarah, he decides to go and sully her

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.280
reputation before she's even had a chance
to establish one at her new school.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.289
He does this by telling everyone that he's
already slept with her just to make himself

00:06:01.289 --> 00:06:02.800
look all big and bro-tastic.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:07.839
Chris is eventually put under a love spell
by Nancy's coven, so he might not be to blame

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.300
for every single one of his acts of desperation.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:14.640
But the curse probably only elevates behaviors
that he is already capable of.

00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:19.400
So when he later tries to force himself on
Sarah after she refuses to sleep with him,

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.460
that is certainly still him being an inappropriate
scumbag, cursed or not.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:28.520
Carter Duncan might be what the title's referring
to in The Perfect Guy, but he is anything

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.020
but.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:33.740
At first, he seems completely handsome and
charming and exactly what Leah needs to get

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.920
over her breakup with her ex-boyfriend Dave.

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:40.419
But when a simple encounter at a gas station
with a stranger turns into a full-on attack

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.620
from her new lover, his true personality reveals
itself.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.560
He's not warm at all; instead, he's vicious
and impetuous and dangerous.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.340
Breaking up is hard to do under even the best
of circumstances, but when a guy has as many

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.100
screws loose as Carter, it's practically impossible.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:08.179
Leah ends up having to recruit her ex to protect
her from Carter as he stalks her at work,

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.780
sneaks into her home, and even steals her
cat.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.040
And that's the tame stuff.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:16.819
Eventually, things turn violent, and Leah
must take matters into her own hands to prevent

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:20.999
him from doing this all again, to her or other
unsuspecting women.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:25.439
If you thought your last Tinder date was terrible,
this guy could make anyone look like "swipe

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.720
right" potential by comparison.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:31.360
It's hard to know what possessed Jenna to
ever date Trent in the first place in the

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.840
Friday the 13th reboot.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:37.279
But a lot of slasher movies don't exactly
work if the characters actually use logic

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:38.400
and make good choices.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:43.550
Trent is spoiled and arrogant and only invites
his "friends" to his parents' lake house to

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.600
show off how wealthy he and his family are.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:48.300
Trent is also completely unkind.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.680
He even starts an argument with a guy who
is only out searching for his missing sister.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:57.420
On top of all those terrible personality traits,
he's also a cheater of the worst order.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:01.599
As soon as Jenna steps away from the lake
house to do a good deed, he hooks up with

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:05.869
her best friend, and their love scene is cringey
enough to make anyone wonder why Jenna gives

00:08:05.869 --> 00:08:07.039
him the time of day.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:11.320
What he says about female anatomy will make
you laugh and cry all at once.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.020
Beauty is only skin deep with this one, that's
for sure.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:19.440
To be fair to The Fly's Seth Brundle, it isn't
necessarily his fault that he's being slowly

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:21.449
morphed into the Brundlefly.

00:08:21.449 --> 00:08:24.669
But that doesn't mean anyone would want to
put up with him once the side effects start

00:08:24.669 --> 00:08:25.200
kicking in.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:31.000
Even before he merges DNA with a horsefly,
Seth is a bit questionable as boyfriend material.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:35.700
Not only is he odd, he's also a bit possessive
of his journalist girlfriend, Ronnie.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:40.800
But Seth becomes most unpleasant after his
little teleportation experiment goes so wrong.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.920
He becomes aggressive and eventually loses
all trace of empathy and emotion.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.660
Instead of protecting Ronnie from the danger
he poses to her, he tries to force her to

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:54.440
carry his baby to term and even attempts to
fuse all three of them together into one entity.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.460
It's bad enough that he gets himself into
this mess by being so sloppy with his work

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:58.960
station.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:03.600
But the fact that he wants to drag his girlfriend
and unborn child down with him makes Seth

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.300
an especially buggin' boyfriend.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:09.940
What's a guy to do do when the woman he loves
is suddenly turned into a Deadite by an ancient

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.280
evil force that's been awoken by a weird book?

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:17.200
For Ash Williams in The Evil Dead, the answer
is to decapitate Linda and then slice her

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.400
still-animated body into bits.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:20.440
What a catch.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:25.470
Never mind the fact that this is all his fault,
as he's the one who brought out the Necronomicon

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.900
and tape reading that set all the hellfire
in motion in the first place.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:34.700
Even if we forgive that, it's his next action
that proves he's completely undateable forever.

00:09:34.709 --> 00:09:39.870
The 2000 video game Evil Dead: Hail to the
King continues the Ash action and shows him

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:44.870
dating a poor girl named Jenny, whom he convinces
to go to the same cabin where all of the crazy

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.660
and terrible things happened before.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:51.740
We're later told she died in an "accident"
with a bus, but that's a little too convenient

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:52.720
to be true, isn't it?

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:57.940
Any time a guy has an alter-ego called "Bad
Ash," it ain't good news.

